23: /**
24:  * Phase 5 T10 — cross-tab outbox ownership and leases (FR-002, FR-004,
25:  * FR-005, BR-003, BR-007; AC-005, AC-006, AC-041, AC-045 E2E cases).
26:  *
27:  * Two real tabs of A (same browser context: one IndexedDB outbox, Web Locks,
28:  * BroadcastChannel) and B on another device. Everything is real: the app, the
29:  * create and fence routes, and the local database. Faults are network shaping
30:  * (SPEC §15): requests held in the browser (delayed pass-through, released
31:  * later with route.fetch), a request failed in transit, the context's offline
32:  * mode, and a database row lock that blocks a create inside its INSERT (as in
33:  * the T2 integration test). A hung tab is a tab whose main thread is paused
34:  * (CDP Debugger.pause): network shaping alone cannot hang a holder
35:  * past its lease, because every request of a claim is aborted at its 30 s
36:  * deadline, before the 45 s lease ends.
37:  */
