The sign-out stop is not stored in shared state. A tab that misses the broadcast, or a write that arrives after the 
purge, can survive it. I also found that the cookie-swap tests close the stale tab before checking its view, so they 
don’t prove that it hides A’s pending content after detecting C’s session.

