codex
The relaxed claim write creates a cancellation risk after an OS crash: IndexedDB can recover the strict initial 
`waiting / generation 0` row even though its create request already left the machine. That row becomes cancellable 
without a fence, while the original request can still commit. This contradicts the claim that losing claim writes is 
harmless.

