286:  * item is ever eligible (BR-003). The caller must hold the conversation's
287:  * drain lock (Web Lock, T10), so any `claimed` item found here belongs to a
288:  * holder that is gone (tab closed or crashed) or whose lease ended (its lock
289:  * was taken over), and is taken over under a newer generation.
290:  *
291:  * Relaxed durability (as for state updates): the write survives a tab or
292:  * browser crash; only an OS crash could lose it, and then the next attempt
293:  * reuses this generation — still exactly once, since the server stores at
294:  * most one message per key and a create first fences older generations.
295:  * Only the item's first write (addOutboxItem) must be flushed (FR-001).
296:  *
297:  * `confirmedKey`: an item of this owner just confirmed by the server, removed
298:  * in the same transaction before the next one is taken. `maxDeferMs`: the
299:  * longest transient backoff; a waiting item whose `retryNotBefore` is at most
300:  * that far ahead is not claimed yet (`deferred`).
