The review requires revisions. Server fencing protects stored-row uniqueness, but the client can still lose the 
dispatched marker, erase a newer claim with an old response, or leave later messages blocked behind a frozen Web Lock. 
The tests miss those interleavings: the hung-tab test resumes the old holder after takeover has finished, and the 
cookie-swap test closes the stale tab before checking what C can see.
